        "isThankYou": false,
        "kernelVersion": 0,
        "parent": {},
        "postDate": "2026-03-31T09:01:33.600Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "Based on my own experience, a larger sample size is not necessarily better, nor is a longer CoT. I am currently still experimenting to determine which specific settings yield the best results. My hypothesis is that this is due to significant distributional shifts between the training and test sets, as well as the presence of noisy data—such as problems that have no valid solution😅",
