      "authorType": "TOPIC",
      "competitionRanking": 1,
      "content": "<p>I trained models with all 9500 samples with/without cot on my local machine. Upload the lora weight to kagge dataset, and submit with the following code:</p>\n<pre><code>import os\nos.chdir('kaggle_lora_path')\n!zip -r /kaggle/working/submission.zip ./*\n</code></pre>\n<p>No mater with/without cot, no matter how many iterations, the score is always lower than 0.6. I noticed that public notebook easily score 0.6x with 600 samples. My score doesn't make any sense! Has anyone faced the same issues and know the reason?</p>\n<p>I just joined this competition two days before, don't downvote me!🤣</p>",
      "feedbackTrackingData": {},
      "id": 3432189,
      "isThankYou": false,
      "kernelVersion": 0,
      "parent": {},
      "postDate": "2026-03-31T07:32:10.987Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "I trained models with all 9500 samples with/without cot on my local machine. Upload the lora weight to kagge dataset, and submit with the following code:\n```\nimport os\nos.chdir('kaggle_lora_path')\n!zip -r /kaggle/working/submission.zip ./*\n```\n\nNo mater with/without cot, no matter how many iterations, the score is always lower than 0.6. I noticed that public notebook easily score 0.6x with 600 samples. My score doesn't make any sense! Has anyone faced the same issues and know the reason?\n\nI just joined this competition two days before, don't downvote me!🤣",
